From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] taskbar: do not render the forced navbar as a taskbar on handhelds

When the user forces the navigation bar on a phone (LineageSettings
FORCE_SHOW_NAVBAR), isTaskbarEnabled() is true but isLargeScreenTaskbar
(DeviceProfile.isTaskbarPresent) is false, and recreateTaskbarForDisplay fell
through to create a taskbar anyway. Its Back/Home/Recents dispatch through the
SystemUiProxy, which does not deliver them here, so the buttons do nothing;
and with SystemUI now drawing its own NavigationBar for phones the two windows
collided (BadTokenException, launcher crash loop). Return early on handhelds so
Launcher creates no taskbar and SystemUI owns the functional navigation bar.

---
 quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarManagerImpl.java | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarManagerImpl.java b/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarManagerImpl.java
--- a/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarManagerImpl.java
+++ b/quickstep/src/com/android/launcher3/taskbar/TaskbarManagerImpl.java
@@ -838,7 +838,11 @@
                 SystemUiProxy systemUiProxy = SystemUiProxy.INSTANCE.get(mBaseContext);
                 systemUiProxy.notifyTaskbarStatus(/* visible */ false, /* stashed */ false);
                 systemUiProxy.setHasBubbleBar(false);
-                if (!isTaskbarEnabled || !displayExists) {
+                // noblelte: a handheld (isLargeScreenTaskbar == false) must not render the
+                // forced navigation bar as a taskbar; SystemUI draws its own functional
+                // 3-button NavigationBar instead. Returning here avoids creating a taskbar
+                // window that would both be non-functional and collide with that bar.
+                if (!isTaskbarEnabled || !displayExists || !isLargeScreenTaskbar) {
                     debugTaskbarManager(
                             "recreateTaskbarForDisplay: exiting bc (!isTaskbarEnabled || "
                                     + "!displayExists)",
-- 
